> Branding and Logo Design - Boon Agency, Gal[way,] Ireland.
Lu[is] and Martina are a Peruvian[ Irish] partnership based in the west of Ireland[. In] 2014[, after living for] ten[ years in] Peru[, they] made[ the] decision[ to return to] Ireland – kids in tow. Armed with their knowledge of Per[uvian] foods,[ they decided] to undertake their dream of introducing quality Andean products[ to] the Irish[ and] European markets.
[In]ca Allpa approached us with a blank page and[ asked us to] create a logo for their new venture. We were instantly drawn to[ the] rich history and culture[ of] Peru and began researching ancient Inc[a] symbols. We decided to create a character[ to] represent the Inc[a] Allpa brand in the style[ of] the Incas. Inc[a] All[pa] are now part of the Superval[u] Food Academy Programme[.]
This project was a challenge and required talent and effort from the design team, the objective was to create a brand that was striking, vibrant and[ in] keeping[ with the] style[ of] the ancient symbols that inspired us. It also has to[ work on] the web, and[ most] importantly[, on] the packaging.
[After weeks of] work and revisions, ‘Diego’ came to life. We love this brand. It is the result of a creative process that[ involves the] client and welcomes feedback.[ The] best results are achieved in this manner.

